  "title": "Only parity survives native patterns of patterns",
  "subject": "Which Boolean knots are rebuilt by native gadgets of their own copies, and what geometry a native law can fix",
  "conclusion": "Among Boolean knots glued natively, only parity is rebuilt by gadgets of its own copies: other three-place knots' gadgets exclude fewer tuples, so towers of patterns of patterns go free within three levels, and at four places (up to three copies) only parity and one chained implication between pair parities survive. No three-place knot orients a vertex and no orienting four-place knot survives, so native laws fix topology but neither orientation nor scale.",
  "authority_class": "proof",
